# The running app's Dock tile keeps the bundled icon on Apple's icon grid, its tile 824 of 1024 px
# with a clear margin, the size of Arc's beside it, also once Chromium's download view takes the
# tile (it draws the bundle's icon under its badge; ⌘-Tab shows that tile). AppIcon.icns was drawn
# edge to edge until 11 Nov 2026 and stood a fifth larger where it was drawn as it is; lint's
# app-icon-grid rule checks the file. Segments (the bundled icon) comes in through the argument
# domain, so the run never writes the installed Cra's defaults. body= and appIcon= are how much of
# the canvas the drawing fills: 81 % on the grid.
home
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true}
arg -appIcon
arg segments
cra://debug?dockTile=before
expect-log dock tile before: view=none appIcon=8[01]%
# A download puts Chromium's view on the tile, drawing the bundled icon under its badge.
cra://open?url=${TRICKLE}/trickle.bin
wait 2
cra://debug?downloadState=started
expect-log download state started: running=true
cra://debug?download=cancel
expect-log download control: cancel
wait 1
cra://debug?dockTile=after
expect-log dock tile after: view=DockTileView .* body=8[01]% appIcon=8[01]%
